<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Braunfels</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Braunfels is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> on a hill above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahn">Lahn</a> near Wetzlar. Its castle, recorded from the 13th century, became the main seat of the counts, later princes, of Solms-Braunfels and was rebuilt in neo-Gothic style in the 19th century. It still belongs to the family and gave its name to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-braunfels">New Braunfels</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/braunfels.jpg" alt="Braunfels" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fritz Geller-Grimm · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Braunfels_Luftbild_051.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
